Description: Mark the downstream build: change notice, MODULE_VERSION, parameter texts
 Adds the dated GPL-2.0 section 2(a) change notice below the upstream
 SPDX line and header, pointing to driver/patches/.
 .
 MODULE_VERSION was "0.2.0" while the package is 0.2.1; it is now the DKMS
 PACKAGE_VERSION "0.2.1+sr1" (packaging/build-deb.sh checks this).
 Resolves F6.
 .
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(force) said "Load read-only without a known Minisforum
 DMI match"; with experimental_write=1 a force-loaded system was writable
 (A2, fixed in 0002). New text: "Bind read-only on an unknown system (never
 enables PWM writes; sensor reads still send EC read commands)". The
 second half states what read-only means here: every temperature or fan
 read writes command bytes to the EC (0x80 to 0x66, 0xd5 plus subcommand
 to 0x6c/0x68). MODULE_PARM_DESC(experimental_write) now carries the risk
 statement and names the allowlist. Resolves A13 (text) and the
 parameter-description part of H3; the README part of H3 is separate.
 .
 Tested: build W=1, sparse, smatch, checkpatch on proxmox-headers
 7.0.14-20-pve and 7.0.12-1-pve (befunde/raw/p4-build-20261009.txt);
 modinfo shows version and parameter texts. No hardware test needed.
Author: SirRenix <7069603+SirRenix@users.noreply.github.com>
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-10-17
---
--- a/driver-prototype/minisforum_n5_it5571.c
+++ b/driver-prototype/minisforum_n5_it5571.c
@@ -19,6 +19,10 @@
  *
  * ACPI EC RAM provides four useful temperature bytes:
  *   0x09 CPU, 0x04 system, 0x05 board/aux, 0x06 ambient.
+ *
+ * Modified 2026-10-17 by SirRenix for the Debian/Proxmox DKMS package
+ * minisforum-n5-it5571-dkms; changes: driver/patches/ in
+ * https://github.com/SirRenix/minisforum-n5pro-fan-proxmox
  */
 
 #include <linux/delay.h>
@@ -50,12 +54,13 @@
 
 static bool force;
 module_param(force, bool, 0444);
-MODULE_PARM_DESC(force, "Load read-only without a known Minisforum DMI match");
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(force,
+		 "Bind read-only on an unknown system (never enables PWM writes; sensor reads still send EC read commands)");
 
 static bool experimental_write;
 module_param(experimental_write, bool, 0444);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(experimental_write,
-		 "Enable PWM writes on experimental or force-loaded systems");
+		 "Enable PWM writes on boards in the downstream write allowlist; experimental, may leave fans at a fixed duty");
 
 struct n5_board_profile {
 	const char *name;
@@ -678,4 +683,4 @@
 MODULE_AUTHOR("ltdstudio, community exploration for the Minisforum N5 family");
 MODULE_DESCRIPTION("Minisforum N5 family IT5571 fan/temp hwmon driver; N5 Pro/Air support is experimental; not affiliated with Minisforum; use at your own risk");
 MODULE_LICENSE("GPL");
-MODULE_VERSION("0.2.0");
+MODULE_VERSION("0.2.1+sr1");
